From: Agent Browser contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Android product audio: clamp capture_time to now (0065)

Device-verified failure on r13u (OnePlus PKG110): a real microphone test
site crashed the renderer three times in a row with
  FATAL media/audio/audio_input_device.cc:491 DCHECK failed:
  now_time >= capture_time (~4us of clock skew)
The browser-side audio clock drifts a few microseconds ahead of the renderer
clock, so buffers captured right after capture start can carry a capture_time
slightly in the future. Official release builds compile this DCHECK out and
report a harmless negative delay; this build runs with DCHECKs enabled.

Fix: define now_time first and clamp capture_time with std::min, keeping the
reported delay monotonic without crashing. Semantics are otherwise
unchanged.

--- a/media/audio/audio_input_device.cc
+++ b/media/audio/audio_input_device.cc
@@ -485,10 +485,16 @@
   // Deliver captured data to the client in floating point format and update
   // the audio delay measurement.
   // TODO(olka, tommi): Take advantage of |capture_time| in the renderer.
+  const base::TimeTicks now_time = base::TimeTicks::Now();
+  // The browser-side audio clock can drift a few microseconds ahead of the
+  // renderer clock, so the first buffers after capture start may carry a
+  // capture_time slightly in the future. Official release builds compile the
+  // DCHECK out and report a harmless negative delay; clamp the capture time
+  // instead so the reported delay stays monotonic without crashing the
+  // renderer (device-verified: a real mic test site hit ~4us of skew).
   const base::TimeTicks capture_time =
-      base::TimeTicks() + base::Microseconds(buffer->params.capture_time_us);
-  const base::TimeTicks now_time = base::TimeTicks::Now();
-  DCHECK_GE(now_time, capture_time);
+      std::min(base::TimeTicks() + base::Microseconds(buffer->params.capture_time_us),
+               now_time);
 
   AudioGlitchInfo glitch_info{
       .duration = base::Microseconds(buffer->params.glitch_duration_us),
